From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zink: no VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo on dma-buf imports with NVIDIA

NVIDIA's proprietary Vulkan driver (L4T R36, 540 branch, Tegra X1) allocates
new, zeroed memory instead of importing when VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR and
VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo are chained into the same vkAllocateMemory. Every
dma-buf Zink imports then reads back empty: a compositor running on Zink shows
client windows as black.

Measured in pure Vulkan on the device: importing a block-linear dma-buf
preserves every byte; adding VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo to the import makes the
image read zero. The driver reports DMA_BUF in exportFromImportedHandleTypes,
so imported memory stays re-exportable without the export structure.

Skip the export structure for imports on NVIDIA proprietary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -1070,8 +1070,15 @@
       emai.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXPORT_MEMORY_ALLOCATE_INFO;
       emai.handleTypes = alloc_info->export_types;
 
-      emai.pNext = mai.pNext;
-      mai.pNext = &emai;
+      /* NVIDIA's proprietary driver (seen on Tegra, 540 branch) allocates new, zeroed memory
+       * instead of importing when an import and VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo share one
+       * allocation, so every imported dma-buf reads back empty. Imported memory can still be
+       * re-exported through exportFromImportedHandleTypes without the export structure.
+       */
+      if (!(alloc_info->whandle && zink_driverid(screen) == VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY)) {
+         emai.pNext = mai.pNext;
+         mai.pNext = &emai;
+      }
       obj->exportable = true;
       obj->exportable_dmabuf = !!(alloc_info->export_types & VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT);
    }
